<title>POLAND: POLAND TO RAISE EXCISE TAX ON CIGARETTES, ALCOHOL.</title>
<headline>POLAND TO RAISE EXCISE TAX ON CIGARETTES, ALCOHOL.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland will raise the excise tax on vodka and cigarettes by nine and 10 percent respectively as of Februry 17, the finance ministry said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It said exice tax on wine and beer would rise by eight percent.</p>
<p>&quot;The rises are as envisaged by the 1997 budget and are necessary to reach the planned budget revenues for this year,&quot; the finance ministry's press office said.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
